    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mt-8 mb-8">Australia: Electronic Transactions Act (ETA)</h1>

    <h2>The ETA Framework</h2>
    <p>In Australia, electronic signatures are legally valid under the Electronic Transactions Act 1999 (ETA) at the federal level, and corresponding ETA legislation in each state and territory.</p>

    <h2>Requirements for Validity</h2>
    <p>To be valid under the ETA, an electronic signature must meet three requirements:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Identity & Intent:</strong> A method must be used to identify the person and indicate their intention in respect of the information communicated.</li>
        <li><strong>Reliability:</strong> The method used must be as reliable as appropriate for the purpose for which the document was generated.</li>
        <li><strong>Consent:</strong> The recipient must consent to the use of the electronic signature method.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>usignpdf's comprehensive <a href="/security/audit-trails">Audit Trail</a> easily satisfies the reliability and identity requirements for most standard commercial transactions.</p>
